screens.prompt:
Screen: Add connection flow shown as a broad 780px focused overlay over a softly dimmed Connections page in the shared shell. Dialog title "Add connection", close icon, helper "Connect an MCP server to this Brain." No five-step wizard.
At top segmented method control "Server URL" / "Paste config" selected / "Approved connector".
Large input area labeled "MCP configuration", fine tabs "Auto-detect" selected / "JSON" / "TOML" / "YAML", light cream monospace editor with small numbered gutter and a short readable JSON example:
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "docs": {
      "url": "https://docs.example.com/mcp",
      "headers": { "Authorization": "Bearer ${DOCS_TOKEN}" }
    }
  }
}
This is an import concept, not existing functionality. Below editor a quiet sage check row "1 server found · HTTP". Adjacent or directly below a clean parsed summary for "docs", target docs.example.com/mcp, runs on "Recollect service" with a small Change link; environment "Brain-wide".
Integrated credentials section headed "Authentication" with options "Secret" selected / "Credential reference" / "None". Labeled password field "DOCS_TOKEN", masked bullet value only, Show icon; storage destination selector "Approved credential provider". One short helper "Stored with the credential provider; excluded from saved config." Never show real secret values or imply Recollect builds a new secret vault.
A tidy optional "Connection name" field containing "Internal docs". Bottom sticky footer with Cancel, outlined "Inspect tools", navy "Review connection". Small line "Imported settings are reviewed before use." No tall narrow form, no repeated help, no useless blank fields, no arbitrary execution or tool calls, no giant warning banners. Excellent spacing and clear grouping. Make this credential-capable setup feel effortless and intentional.
